    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) stands as our premier offensive weapon, benefiting from an elite matchup against Sugano. The combination of a high-ceiling SP_xERA and a leadoff spot against a righty creates a perfect environment for **Lawrence Butler** to provide the speed and counting stats we crave. **Taylor Ward** (70.31) and **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) are our next most efficient options; **Taylor Ward** gains significant value from a favorable park factor against Buehler, while **Jonathan Aranda** remains a high-floor play given his impressive 0.378 xwOBA, which anchors his strong score despite facing a tough opponent in Rodriguez.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Bryson Stott**, who narrowly missed the starting lineup with a 37.77 efficiency score. While **Bryson Stott** typically provides a stabilizing presence, the combination of a difficult matchup against Harrison and the strict 40-point efficiency floor necessitated by our game cap management kept him on the bench. We are also heavily monitoring the absence of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Cal Raleigh**, and **Yainer Diaz**, whose IL designations continue to force us into secondary options like **Gavin Sheets** and **Drew Gilbert**. While **Gavin Sheets** (58.50) is nearing an elite efficiency tier, **Drew Gilbert** (40.12) is teetering on the edge of our viability threshold; he will be the first player monitored should we need to shuffle for late-breaking weather or lineup changes. \n\nBeyond our core starters, we are keeping a close eye on the secondary tier of **Geraldo Perdomo** (69.29) and **Jeremiah Jackson** (65.88). Both players are benefiting from strong SP_xERA profiles today, making them essential pivots if we hope to maintain our pace in stolen bases. With **Luis Arraez** (54.20) and **Matt Chapman** (55.43) rounding out the infield, our lineup is balanced to exploit the specific weaknesses of the day\u2019s opposing starters. We remain cautious regarding the platoon risks for **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Drew Gilbert** against Rolison, but current projections suggest that sticking to our disciplined rotation strategy\u2014leaving **Bryson Stott** and our injured stars like **Will Smith**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Masyn Winn**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Gleyber Torres**, and **Ryan Waldschmidt** out of the active mix\u2014is the most efficient path to maximizing our daily roto output.",
